{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Pass legislation to allow people to block themselves from alcohol purchases ",
        "additional_details": "We call on the Government to amend the Licensing Act 2003 and the Digital Identity and Attributes Trust Framework to create a legally binding, voluntary alcohol self-exclusion system across online and physical retail to accomplish this.\r\n \r\nCurrent UK law allows citizens to legally self-exclude from gambling, but no framework exists for those recovering from alcohol dependency. While digital IDs are now legally accepted for age verification, they lack a mechanism to enforce self-exclusion.\r\n",
        "background": "Mandate that certified Digital ID providers offer an opt-in Alcohol Self-Exclusion Flag. When scanned at checkouts/bars, it would automatically block the sale & give retailers clear legal backing to refuse service & would empower people in recovery to protect themselves using existing digital tools.",
